      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the proficiency of pediatricians in the demonstration of the proper use of metered-dose inhalers (MDIs) and to assess their theoretical knowledge of inhalation devices used in the management of asthma."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Prospective cross-sectional survey."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "Two university-affiliated hospitals."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PARTICIPANTS",
          "content": "Seventy-one pediatricians and pediatric house staff."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "Each pediatrician's technique was graded by two trained observers using a checklist of six essential steps recommended by national guidelines. Theoretical knowledge of asthma devices was evaluated by a written questionnaire."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Twenty (35.2%) pediatricians performed at least five steps correctly, 28 (39.4%) performed three or four steps correctly, and 18 (25.4%) performed two steps or less correctly. The most common errors were failure to start inhalation from functional residual capacity, failure to inhale slowly, and failure to wait at least 20 seconds before the next puff. Senior pediatricians were more skillful in the practical use of MDIs than were pediatric house staff (p = 0.03). The most common deficiencies in theoretical knowledge were related to estimation of the amount of medication in the canister (8.5% correct) and how valved holding chambers (VHCs) improve drug delivery to the lung (15.5% correct)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Pediatricians in Kuwait have significant deficiencies regarding the practical and theoretical aspects of MDIs and other inhalation devices."
        }
      ]},
